<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 16 December, from 714 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">714 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,312 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pepin of Herstal, ruler of the Franks, dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal">Pepin of Herstal</a>, the mayor of the palace who held real power over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Frankish kingdoms</a>, died at Jupille. After a struggle, his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> took control and laid the ground for the Carolingian dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal">Pepin of Herstal</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">755 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,271 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An Lushan launches his rebellion against the Tang</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a>, a Tang frontier general of Sogdian and Turkic descent, rose in revolt against his rival, the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-guozhong">Yang Guozhong</a>. The rebellion lasted until 763, captured both Tang capitals and permanently weakened central authority.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-guozhong">Yang Guozhong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1431">1431 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">595 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VI is crowned king of France in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The ten-year-old Henry VI of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> at Notre-Dame. By 1453 the English had lost all their French lands except Calais.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1598">1598 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">428 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Admiral Yi Sun-sin is killed in the victory at Noryang</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A combined Korean and Ming fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yi-sun-sin">Yi Sun-sin</a> and Chen Lin attacked Japanese ships gathering in the Noryang Strait to withdraw, sinking a large number. Yi was killed in this last major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imjin-war">Imjin War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-noryang">Battle of Noryang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yi-sun-sin">Yi Sun-sin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imjin-war">Imjin War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1773">1773 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">253 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Boston Tea Party</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonists, some disguised as Mohawk Indians, boarded three ships in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> Harbor and threw 342 chests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> into the water. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s punitive response pushed the colonies towards revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1838">1838 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">188 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Voortrekkers defeat a Zulu army at Blood River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A laager of about 470 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> repelled thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> warriors sent by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane</a> at the Ncome River. The victory became a central symbol of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaner</a> nationalism.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany launches the Battle of the Bulge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces attacked through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and Luxembourg, catching the Americans by surprise. The offensive was contained within weeks and used up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s last reserves in the west.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kazakhstan declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Kazakhstan became the last Soviet republic to declare independence, days before the USSR was dissolved. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nursultan-nazarbayev">Nursultan Nazarbayev</a> led the vast Central Asian country for nearly three decades.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 16 December <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-iii-of-trebizond"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-iii-of-trebizond.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel III of Trebizond</span><span class="tp">1364–1417</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-silang"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Diego Silang</span><span class="tp">1730–1763</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gebhard Leberecht von Blücher</span><span class="tp">1742–1819</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-van-beethoven"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludwig-van-beethoven.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludwig van Beethoven</span><span class="tp">1770–1827</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jane-austen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jane-austen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jane Austen</span><span class="tp">1775–1817</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anton-denikin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anton Denikin</span><span class="tp">1872–1947</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 16 December <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pippin-of-herstal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pippin-of-herstal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pippin of Herstal</span><span class="tp">c. 635–714</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ranulf-de-gernon-4th-earl-of-chester"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ranulf-de-gernon-4th-earl-of-chester.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ranulf de Gernon, 4th Earl of Chester</span><span class="tp">d. 1153</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/haakon-iv-of-norway"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/haakon-iv-of-norway.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Haakon IV of Norway</span><span class="tp">1204–1263</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/afonso-de-albuquerque"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/afonso-de-albuquerque.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Afonso de Albuquerque</span><span class="tp">c. 1453–1515</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yi-sun-sin"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Yi Sun-sin</span><span class="tp">1545–1598</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gabriel-narutowicz"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gabriel-narutowicz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gabriel Narutowicz</span><span class="tp">1865–1922</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
